naval-infinity = "2021-07-02 · The Beginning of Infinity, Part 1 · https://nav.al/infinity · Naval and Brett Hall; collects the short Feb–Jul 2021 episodes below. Naval: science drives progress and is the study of truth; verify ideas yourself (nullius in verba); reread core works rather than skimming many; good explanations are testable, hard to vary, make risky predictions; induction fails (the turkey); knowledge lives in the knower; Bayesian updating suits known options, not new explanations; pessimism is self-fulfilling and rational optimism fits the evidence; entrepreneurs get better feedback than academics; any child could make breakthroughs. Hall: reality is comprehensible and problems soluble; all knowledge, including mathematics, is conjectural; explanation precedes prediction; quantum theory implies a multiverse; science never ends; probability is subjective."
